# ...and the SUFFIXED forms, which are the ones this project actually writes.
# `*.bak` matches a file whose name ENDS in `.bak`; every backup convention in
# use here appends a reason and a date after it --
# `.bak_20260807_disclosure_scrub`, `.bak.d7_clock_skew_removal.20260806T175404Z`
# -- so none of them were covered.
#
# Measured on 2026-08-07: 130 such files sat untracked and unignored, and 24 of
# them carried 80 infrastructure-address occurrences. They are the PRE-SCRUB
# originals written by the disclosure-scrub lanes. So every scrub was leaving a
# verbatim copy of exactly what it had just removed, one `git add -A` away from
# the index -- the cleanup and its own undo, side by side. Backups are worth
# keeping; they are not worth committing.
*.bak_*
*.bak.*
*.orig_*
*.orig.*
